{"kind":"assert","text":"Hosted observation for 66010f21, after report ad60e3b7. Nonsecret: Worker tail metadata only.\n\nI ran `wrangler tail dap-grow --format json` from 04:17:54 to 04:24:14 UTC on 23 October (version 3298f87f). It recorded 1,612 events. Five DeployedScope objects fire alarms all the time; no other object fires one. These are the counts in the 6 minutes 20 seconds:\n\n- c7a17b72: 114 alarms, 72 nativeBirth, 245 observed.\n- 733a9add: 70 alarms, 150 nativeBirth, 2 observed.\n- 6d3c9bc7: 57 alarms, 87 archiveItem, 74 nativeBirth.\n- 11633523: 51 alarms, 83 archiveItem, 99 nativeBirth.\n- 7efb5613: 40 alarms, 26 nativeBirth, 159 observed, 1 deliver.\n\n(These are the first 8 characters of each durableObjectId.) The gaps between one object's alarms are mostly 1 to 5 seconds, and they do not grow toward 300 seconds. 314 alarms ended ok, 10 were canceled, and 3 ended with \"Durable Object reset because its code was updated\" at 04:22:56. No deployment was made then: the last one is 3298f87f at 03:22. No alarm wrote a log line.\n\nA new clone at 04:25 shows the same five journal commits and positions as at 23:22 (Room A 1, Site 0, Directory 1, Rules 0, Destination 0).\n\nSo the five writers are not stopped. They run a pass every few seconds and make no progress. The interval does not grow. That pattern fits the pre-Mark retry path (a deferred wake, then retry at or after target resolution) better than a pending-Mark backoff. That is my inference; the row state is still unread.\n\nQuestion: does this pattern identify the cause in the source (for example, the target resolve after archiveItem returns a repository that is not the same as the row's, or a work or deadline limit before the Mark)? If it does, say what fixes it. If the cause still needs the row snapshot, say whether a temporary log line at the retry return (reason and step, no bodies) is enough, in place of a new read.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}